d arbitrary classes, but I'm moving toward a cleaner approach. Using `translate-y` with responsive prefixes seems promising. I'm exploring the best way to handle large screens, considering that `xl:mt-12` might be simpler than other strategies. I'm thinking about laptop and large screen dimensions, considering the proper prefix to use (lg, xl, or 2xl).\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Use responsive standard Tailwind classes to push hero down on large screens","EndLine":219,"Instruction":"Remove inline style and use responsive translate classes","ReplacementContent":"        {/* ── Headline — fills remaining space, anchored to bottom ── */}\n        <div className=\"flex-1 flex flex-col justify-center pb-[22vh] -translate-y-12 2xl:translate-y-4\">","StartLine":217,"TargetContent":"        {/* ── Headline — fills remaining space, anchored to bottom ── */}\n        <div className=\"flex-1 flex flex-col justify-center pb-[22vh]\" style={{ transform: \"translateY(-6vh)\" }}>","TargetFile":"/home/clouder/Documents/projects/buildroot/front-buildroot/components/home/Hero.tsx","toolAction":"Apply responsive translation","toolSummary":"File edit"}}]}
