{"step_index":708,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-07-24T02:29:13Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, emphasizing specific tools over general ones where possible. The goal is to optimize efficiency by leveraging tools like 'view_file' directly, rather than resorting to broader, less direct methods. I'm aiming for targeted actions.\n\n\n**Analyzing Image Distortion**\n\nI've pinpointed the image blur issue to how the canvas dimensions are handled during animation. The `canvas.clientWidth` is minuscule when `img.onload` fires, causing the image to render at a low resolution and stretch afterward. This is due to the `motion.div` animation. The canvas must determine its final resolution, not its initial animating resolution.\n\n\n**Optimizing Canvas Resolution**\n\nI've decided to set the canvas's internal resolution to the image's natural dimensions, abandoning the previous approach. By setting `canvas.width = img.naturalWidth` and using CSS `object-cover`, the canvas maintains high quality, and CSS handles the scaling responsively. This means that the pixel size will be based on the natural image size.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Fix canvas resolution being small during animation by using native image dimensions","EndLine":30,"Instruction":"Change canvas width and height initialization to use img.naturalWidth and img.naturalHeight so it doesn't get a 0 width during the motion layout animation","ReplacementContent":"    img.onload = () => {\n      // Use the image's raw high-resolution dimensions for the canvas internal buffer\n      // This prevents the canvas from capturing a tiny width while the CSS animation is opening it\n      canvas.width = img.naturalWidth;\n      canvas.height = img.naturalHeight;\n      \n      const width = canvas.width;\n      const height = canvas.height;\n\n      const draw = (pixelSize: number) => {\n        ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n        // When pixelSize is 1 or less, draw the crisp high-res image\n        if (pixelSize <= 1.05) {\n          ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = true; // Enable smoothing for the crisp final photo\n          ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, width, height);\n          return;\n        }","StartLine":19,"TargetContent":"    img.onload = () => {\n      // Use devicePixelRatio to ensure Retina crispness\n      const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 2;\n      const width = canvas.clientWidth;\n      const height = canvas.clientHeight;\n      \n      canvas.width = width * dpr;\n      canvas.height = height * dpr;\n\n      const draw = (pixelSize: number) => {\n        ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n\n        // When pixelSize is 1 or less, draw the crisp high-res image\n        if (pixelSize <= 1.05) {\n          ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = true; // Enable smoothing for the crisp final photo\n          ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n          return;\n        }","TargetFile":"/home/clouder/Documents/projects/buildroot/front-buildroot/components/ui/PixelImage.tsx","toolAction":"Fix Canvas Resolution","toolSummary":"File edit"}}]}
