{"step_index":723,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-07-24T02:30:53Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, emphasizing specific tools over general ones where possible. The goal is to optimize efficiency by leveraging tools tailored to particular tasks, like viewing files. This strategy promises a more targeted and less error-prone approach to problem-solving, which I will continue to refine and implement moving forward.\n\n\n**Refining Execution Protocols**\n\nI'm now integrating new rules to optimize tool usage. I'm focusing on avoiding `cat` for file creation/appending and prioritizing `grep_search` over `grep` within commands. Further, I'm now explicitly listing related tools before tool calls. This will smooth out my approach, as now I will be more focused in the tool selection stage.\n\n\n**Analyzing Smooth Despixelation**\n\nI'm now diving deep into smoothing the despixelation process. I'm seeing that shrinking blocks cause a visual stutter. The goal is now liquid/cinematic. I'm focusing on either a crossfade with opacity or CSS blur with contrast. The key seems to be avoiding the direct, mechanical animation of block sizes, as that's very jarring.\n\n\n**Optimizing Pixel Rendering**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the \"mechanized\" look of the pixelation. The issue arises from discrete jumps in block counts due to `Math.floor()`. Using floating point values for scaled dimensions offers a potential fix, but canvas integer limitations present a challenge. My new plan is to smoothly fade between the images instead.\n\n\n**Implementing Smooth Pixelation**\n\nI'm now investigating achieving smooth pixelation. My initial idea of using `blur` is off, the user wants pixelation. I'm focusing on either a crossfade with opacity or a multi-phase discrete pixelation approach. The most promising seems to be drawing the pixelated image in the background, and then crossfading a sharp image on top, with both block sizes and the crossfade being animated. This appears to mask the block jitter.\n\n\n**Finalizing Crossfade Strategy**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a crossfade technique to ensure smooth pixelation transitions. I've decided to animate `pixelSize` from an initial large value to 1. I'll draw the pixelated image, and then overlay the sharp version with `globalAlpha` set to `1 - (pixelSize - 1) / (initialPixelSize - 1)`. As `pixelSize` decreases, the sharp image will fade in, effectively masking any block jitter. This is now being implemented within `PixelImage.tsx`.\n\n\n**Refining Pixel Dissolve**\n\nI'm now implementing the smooth \"melting\" transition for pixelation. The approach focuses on an on-screen crossfade for animation. A pixelated image is drawn first, then overlaid with a sharp image that fades in via alpha, as the pixel size decreases. The current update involves calculating the progress for the smooth fade-in, and implementing the easing curve for alpha. This strategy is proving highly effective in obscuring the \"mechanical\" nature of the pixel block resizing.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Implement a crossfade to make the pixelation smooth and cinematic","EndLine":48,"Instruction":"Add a crossfade logic by drawing the sharp image on top of the pixelated canvas using globalAlpha based on animation progress","ReplacementContent":"        if (offCtx) {\n          offCtx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, scaledW, scaledH);\n          \n          // Draw the pixelated blocks\n          ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;\n          ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n          ctx.drawImage(offscreen, 0, 0, width, height);\n        }\n\n        // SMOOTHING MAGIC: Crossfade the perfectly sharp image on top \n        // This hides the 'mechanical' jitter of the resizing blocks and makes it melt\n        const initialPixelSize = Math.max(40, Math.floor(width / 10));\n        const progress = 1 - ((pixelSize - 1) / (initialPixelSize - 1));\n        \n        // Exponential fade-in for buttery smoothness\n        ctx.globalAlpha = progress * progress * progress; \n        ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = true;\n        ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, width, height);\n        \n        // Reset alpha for next frame\n        ctx.globalAlpha = 1;\n      };","StartLine":42,"TargetContent":"        if (offCtx) {\n          offCtx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, scaledW, scaledH);\n          \n          // Draw the tiny canvas back onto the main canvas, scaled up to fill the high-res bounds\n          ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false; // Disable smoothing to show crisp square blocks\n          ctx.drawImage(offscreen, 0, 0, width, height);\n        }\n      };","TargetFile":"/home/clouder/Documents/projects/buildroot/front-buildroot/components/ui/PixelImage.tsx","toolAction":"Smooth pixelation","toolSummary":"File edit"}}]}
