{"step_index":1729,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-07-24T23:52:39Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI'm now focusing on tool selection, emphasizing specific tools over general ones where possible. The goal is to optimize efficiency by leveraging tools like 'view_file' directly, rather than resorting to broader, less direct methods. I'm aiming for targeted actions.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Choices**\n\nI'm recalling critical instruction 1 and 2 to inform my approach. Specifically, I'm choosing `replace_file_content` to adjust the loader logic in `Preloader.tsx` to ensure only the `buildroot_` loading screen appears, a focused and direct method.\n\n\n**Clarifying Loading Behavior**\n\nI'm now focusing on the user's requirement for the `buildroot_` preloader. I need to ensure it reappears on homepage reloads, but only the `buildroot_` image, not the additional words. The existing `sessionStorage` logic prevents this, as the preloader currently runs only once per session. I'm trying to determine when those floating words appear. The user wants to avoid them when reloading the home page.\n\n\n**Interpreting Reload Preference**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the exact behavior for homepage reloads. The user's phrasing, \"solo buildroot en este caso,\" strongly suggests they want *only* the `buildroot_` image to appear on reloads, *never* the floating words. I'm inferring a preference for a focused, streamlined reload experience, and that the \"floating words\" are not wanted. I'm moving toward the conclusion that I must remove them.\n\n\n**Confirming User Intent**\n\nI'm now clarifying the user's explicit preference for homepage reloads. The phrasing \"solo buildroot\" and \"cuando se recarga el home\" confirms they *only* want the `buildroot_` preloader image to appear upon homepage reloads. I'm moving forward with a plan to remove the floating words and ensure the preloader shows consistently on `/` reloads. I'm leaning toward using `usePathname` from `next/navigation` to detect if we are on the Home page.\n\n\n**Distinguishing First Visit**\n\nI'm now determining the user's intended initial load behavior versus reloads. They DO want the full preloader, *including* the floating words, on the *very first* session visit. Subsequent visits to `/` require *only* the `buildroot_` image. I'm planning to use `sessionStorage` for a \"first_visit\" flag, and then conditionally render components using `isFirstVisit` and `usePathname` from `next/navigation`.\n\n\n**Interpreting Navigation Behavior**\n\nI'm now clarifying the impact of client-side navigation on preloader behavior. The user's intent is for the preloader to appear only on a full page reload or initial load of `/`, not on client-side navigation to `/` from `/services`. The `<Link>` component on navigation should *not* show the preloader. I'm focusing on ensuring the `useEffect` within `Preloader` only runs on a hard refresh, confirming the use of `sessionStorage`. My conclusion is that \"recarga\" signifies a hard refresh or initial visit.\n\n\n**Addressing Navigation Effects**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a critical issue: the `useEffect` within `Preloader` is triggered by client-side navigation because `pathname` is in the dependency array. This violates the user's intent to display the preloader *only* on a hard refresh (or first visit). I'm concluding that removing `pathname` from the dependency array will fix the problem. I will also need to re-evaluate the navigation behavior.\n\n\n**Analyzing Navigation Behavior**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on optimizing the preloader behavior with client-side navigation. My current plan is to only trigger the check for the preloader *once* on component mount, which I can achieve with a blank dependency array. I will use `window.location.pathname` within the mount effect, guaranteeing this check only runs on the initial load or a hard refresh. I now plan to use `sessionStorage` in order to track first visits.\n\n```\nI'm now zeroing in on optimizing the preloader behavior with client-side navigation. My current plan is to only trigger the check for the preloader *once* on component mount, which I can achieve with a blank dependency array. I will use `window.location.pathname` within the mount effect, guaranteeing this check only runs on the initial load or a hard refresh. I now plan to use `sessionStorage` in order to track first visits.\n```\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Modify Preloader to show only buildroot on home reload","EndLine":144,"Instruction":"Update Preloader logic to use `isFirstVisit` state. If first visit, show full animation for 2.6s. If subsequent visit BUT hard reload on \"/\", show only buildroot for 1.2s. Otherwise, show nothing.","ReplacementContent":"export function Preloader() {\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [showPreloader, setShowPreloader] = useState(false);\n  const [isFirstVisit, setIsFirstVisit] = useState(false);\n  const [activeItems, setActiveItems] = useState<number[]>([]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const hasVisited = sessionStorage.getItem(\"buildroot_visited\");\n    \n    if (!hasVisited) {\n      setIsFirstVisit(true);\n      setShowPreloader(true);\n      sessionStorage.setItem(\"buildroot_visited\", \"true\");\n      \n      const timers = floatingItems.flatMap((item) => [\n        setTimeout(() => setActiveItems((prev) => [...prev, item.id]), item.start),\n        setTimeout(() => setActiveItems((prev) => prev.filter((id) => id !== item.id)), item.end),\n      ]);\n      \n      timers.push(setTimeout(() => setIsLoading(false), 2600));\n      \n      return () => timers.forEach(clearTimeout);\n    } else if (window.location.pathname === \"/\") {\n      setIsFirstVisit(false);\n      setShowPreloader(true);\n      \n      const timer = setTimeout(() => setIsLoading(false), 1200);\n      return () => clearTimeout(timer);\n    } else {\n      setShowPreloader(false);\n      setIsLoading(false);\n    }\n  }, []);\n\n  if (!showPreloader) return null;\n\n  return (\n    <AnimatePresence>\n      {isLoading && (\n        <motion.div\n          key=\"preloader\"\n          initial={{ y: 0 }}\n          exit={{ y: \"-100%\" }}\n          transition={{ duration: 0.9, ease: [0.76, 0, 0.24, 1] }}\n          className=\"fixed inset-0 z-[100] flex items-center justify-center bg-[var(--text-primary)] text-[var(--bg-primary)] overflow-hidden\"\n        >\n          {/* Main Logo Center */}\n          <div className=\"absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center pointer-events-none z-10\">\n            <div className=\"overflow-hidden\">\n              <motion.div\n                initial={{ y: \"100%\" }}\n                animate={{ y: 0 }}\n                transition={{ duration: 0.6, ease: [0.76, 0, 0.24, 1] }}\n                className=\"font-mono text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-[6rem] font-light tracking-tighter flex items-center\"\n              >\n                <ScrambleText text=\"buildroot\" speed={60} trigger=\"mount\" />\n                <motion.span\n                  initial={{ opacity: 0 }}\n                  animate={{ opacity: [0, 1, 0] }}\n                  transition={{ repeat: Infinity, duration: 0.8, ease: \"linear\" }}\n                  className=\"inline-block scale-y-75 origin-bottom ml-1\"\n                >\n                  _\n                </motion.span>\n              </motion.div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          {/* Floating Texts - ONLY SHOW ON VERY FIRST VISIT */}\n          {isFirstVisit && (\n            <div className=\"absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none\">\n              <AnimatePresence>\n                {floatingItems.map((item) => (\n                  activeItems.includes(item.id) && (\n                    <motion.div\n                      key={`loc-${item.id}`}\n                      className={`absolute flex flex-col font-mono text-[10px] md:text-xs font-light uppercase tracking-[0.2em] opacity-70 ${item.className}`}\n                      initial={{ opacity: 0.7 }}\n                      animate={{ opacity: 0.7 }}\n                      exit={{ opacity: 0 }}\n                      transition={{ duration: 0.2 }}\n                    >\n                      <span><ScrambleText text={item.line1} speed={25} trigger=\"mount\" /></span>\n                      <span><ScrambleText text={item.line2} speed={25} trigger=\"mount\" /></span>\n                    </motion.div>\n                  )\n                ))}\n              </AnimatePresence>\n            </div>\n          )}\n        </motion.div>\n      )}\n    </AnimatePresence>\n  );\n}","StartLine":49,"TargetContent":"export function Preloader() {\n  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [showPreloader, setShowPreloader] = useState(false);\n  const [activeItems, setActiveItems] = useState<number[]>([]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const hasVisited = sessionStorage.getItem(\"buildroot_visited\");\n    \n    if (!hasVisited) {\n      setShowPreloader(true);\n      sessionStorage.setItem(\"buildroot_visited\", \"true\");\n      \n      const timers = floatingItems.flatMap((item) => [\n        setTimeout(() => setActiveItems((prev) => [...prev, item.id]), item.start),\n        setTimeout(() => setActiveItems((prev) => prev.filter((id) => id !== item.id)), item.end),\n      ]);\n      \n      timers.push(setTimeout(() => setIsLoading(false), 2600));\n      \n      return () => timers.forEach(clearTimeout);\n    } else {\n      setShowPreloader(false);\n      setIsLoading(false);\n    }\n  }, []);\n\n  if (!showPreloader) return null;\n\n  return (\n    <AnimatePresence>\n      {isLoading && (\n        <motion.div\n          key=\"preloader\"\n          initial={{ y: 0 }}\n          exit={{ y: \"-100%\" }}\n          transition={{ duration: 0.9, ease: [0.76, 0, 0.24, 1] }}\n          className=\"fixed inset-0 z-[100] flex ite